title: Below the first layer there is nothing to integrate, only something to notice.
pid: b31646b5-f989-48d3-9471-88408db2b500
body: |2-
  B is shared, so C2 is in A' the moment it exists. Deep reporting is a
  problem of notices and receipts, not of merging. The exception is a
  node below that one has forked: it has its own subscription, and its
  count does not rise to the fork above it.
